IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `la-dates`

-- Limitation Act 2005 (WA) -- the rules a person bringing (or answering) a claim meets: Part 1 (ss 4, 6, 6A, 6B, 7),
-- Part 2 so far as it fixes the periods for personal injury, death, trespass to the person, contribution, deeds and the
-- general 6 years (ss 12-14, 16-18), Part 3 (extension for minors and persons with a mental disability, extension by
-- courts, by agreement and by confirmation, ss 30-53 except s 54), Part 4 Division 1 for personal injury and dust
-- diseases (ss 55-57), Part 6 ss 79 and 81, and Part 7 (child sexual abuse actions, ss 89-92).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in la-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("cannot be commenced if",
-- "means", "is of no effect unless", "is not to extend time ... unless", "may not", an "if" or "when" condition that
-- fails); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The court's
-- judgments ("satisfied", "reasonable", "just and reasonable") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a
-- guess at them. Periods are counted with the day of the event excluded, so the last day to commence is the anniversary
-- (forks F1, F2 in NOTES.md).
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "Limitation Act 2005", State of Western
-- Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 2005`

§§ `Part 1 -- application`

-- s 3(1): "commencement day means the day on which this Act comes into operation"; s 2: Royal Assent; the compilation
-- table: assent and commencement 15 November 2005.
`the commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 11 2005

-- s 89: "commencement day means the day on which the Civil Liability Legislation Amendment (Child Sexual Abuse Actions)
-- Act 2018 section 12 comes into operation" -- 1 July 2018 (compilation table).
`the Part 7 commencement day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2018

-- s 56(1)(b): "a person who did not have knowledge of the relevant facts before 1 January 1984".
`the 1984 knowledge day` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 1984

-- The kinds of action the encoding answers. Part 2 Division 3 gives each but the last its own period; the last takes the
-- general period of Division 2 (s 13). Land, mortgages, defamation, accounts, equitable actions, tax and arbitration
-- (ss 15, 19-29) are not in the focus and are answered "not answered by this encoding".
DECLARE `Kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `damages for a personal injury`
    `a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 action for a death`
    `trespass to the person, assault, battery or imprisonment`
    `contribution between tortfeasors`
    `an action on a deed`
    `any other cause of action`
    `land, a mortgage, defamation, an account, an equitable claim, tax or an arbitration`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the encoding covers` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `land, a mortgage, defamation, an account, an equitable claim, tax or an arbitration` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Whether Part 2 Division 3 provides the period (ss 14, 16, 17, 18), or Division 2 (s 13).
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 3 provides the period for` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `any other cause of action` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `land, a mortgage, defamation, an account, an equitable claim, tax or an arbitration` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The Part 2 period, in years.
-- s 13(1): "6 years have elapsed since the cause of action accrued".
-- s 14(1): personal injury, "3 years have elapsed since the cause of action accrued"; s 14(2): Fatal Accidents Act 1959,
-- "3 years have elapsed since the death" (for that kind the day given is the day of the death).
-- s 16: trespass to the person, assault, battery, imprisonment, 3 years. s 17: contribution, 2 years. s 18: deed, 12 years.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part 2 period in years for` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `damages for a personal injury` THEN 3
    WHEN `a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 action for a death` THEN 3
    WHEN `trespass to the person, assault, battery or imprisonment` THEN 3
    WHEN `contribution between tortfeasors` THEN 2
    WHEN `an action on a deed` THEN 12
    WHEN `any other cause of action` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`, `the accrual day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Part 2 -- the last day for` k `accrued on` `the accrual day` MEANS
    `the anniversary` (`the Part 2 period in years for` k) `years after` `the accrual day`

§§ `ss 6A, 90 -- child sexual abuse actions`

-- s 6A(1): "child means a person under 18 years of age; child sexual abuse, of a person, means an act or omission in
-- relation to the person, when the person is a child, that is sexual abuse; ... child sexual abuse cause of action means a
-- cause of action that relates, directly or indirectly, to a personal injury of the person to whom the cause of action
-- accrues, where the injury results from child sexual abuse of the person." (6): it "does not include a cause of action,
-- action on which could not be maintained but for the Fatal Accidents Act 1959 or the Law Reform (Miscellaneous
-- Provisions) Act 1941." "Sexual abuse" is not defined: asked as a fact. A "means" definition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `the injury results from sexual abuse of me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was under 18 when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it could be brought only because of the Fatal Accidents Act or the survival Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6A(1), (6) -- it is a child sexual abuse action` `the injury results from sexual abuse of me` `I was under 18 when it happened` `it could be brought only because of the Fatal Accidents Act or the survival Act` MEANS
    IF `the injury results from sexual abuse of me` AND `I was under 18 when it happened` AND (NOT `it could be brought only because of the Fatal Accidents Act or the survival Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3 -- the facts of one claim`

-- One claim, from the seat of the person to whom the cause of action accrues.
DECLARE `The claim` HAS
    `claim kind`                                IS A `Kind of action`
    `claim is a child sexual abuse action`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim is a subsequent dust disease action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim accrual day`                         IS A DATE
    `claimant birth day`                        IS A DATE
    `claim came on the death of a minor or disabled person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days without a guardian while under 18`    IS A NUMBER
    `close relationship while under 18`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `mental disability after accrual`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `days without a guardian while disabled`    IS A NUMBER
    `close relationship while disabled`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `close relationship has ceased`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `close relationship ceased on`              IS A DATE

-- What the limitation period comes to.
DECLARE `Time limit` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period applies`
    `the last day to commence is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the law before 15 November 2005 decides`
    `not answered by this encoding`

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`the Part 2 last day of` c MEANS `Part 2 -- the last day for` (c's `claim kind`) `accrued on` (c's `claim accrual day`)

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant was under 18 at accrual` c IF
    (c's `claim accrual day`) `is before` (`the day of reaching age` 18 `for birth on` (c's `claimant birth day`))

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claimant was under 15 at accrual` c IF
    (c's `claim accrual day`) `is before` (`the day of reaching age` 15 `for birth on` (c's `claimant birth day`))

-- s 53(2): where the cause of action of a person who died under 18, or with a mental disability, accrues on the death to a
-- person under 18 or with a mental disability, "a further extension of time is not allowed by reason of person B's being
-- under 18 years of age or suffering a mental disability." The encoding then ignores the claimant's own age and disability.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 1 extends the claim` c IF
    `the claimant was under 18 at accrual` c AND (NOT (c's `claim came on the death of a minor or disabled person`))

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 2 extends the claim` c IF
    c's `mental disability after accrual` AND (NOT (c's `claim came on the death of a minor or disabled person`))

§§ `Part 3 Division 1 -- persons under 18 when the cause of action accrues (ss 30-33)`

-- s 30(1): under 15 at accrual: "cannot be commenced if 6 years have elapsed since the cause of action accrued". (2): "does
-- not apply if Part 2 Division 3 provides for a longer limitation period".
-- s 31(1): 15, 16 or 17 at accrual: "cannot be commenced if the person has reached 21 years of age". (2): "does not apply
-- if Part 2 Division 2 or 3 provides for a longer limitation period".
-- s 32(1): time after accrual and before 18 during which the person "is without a guardian ... does not count"; (2)
-- "Despite subsection (1), an action ... cannot be commenced -- (a) if the person has reached 21 years of age; or (b) in
-- the case where Part 2 Division 2 or 3 provides for a longer limitation period ..., if that limitation period has
-- expired." (3): "subject to section 33".
-- s 33(1): a defendant "in a close relationship" with the person at any time after accrual and before 18: "cannot be
-- commenced if person A has reached 25 years of age". (2): "does not apply if Part 2 Division 3 provides for a longer
-- limitation period". Read as replacing ss 30 to 32 where it applies (finding 2, fork F4).
-- A "longer" period is compared by the day it ends (fork F3).
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`Division 1 -- the last day of` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF c's `close relationship while under 18`
        THEN IF `Division 3 provides the period for` (c's `claim kind`) AND ((`the Part 2 last day of` c) `is after` `the day before 25`)
             THEN `the Part 2 last day of` c
             ELSE `the day before 25`
        IF `the claimant was under 15 at accrual` c
        THEN IF `Division 3 provides the period for` (c's `claim kind`) AND ((`the Part 2 last day of` c) `is after` `the section 30 day`)
             THEN `the Part 2 last day of` c
             ELSE `the earlier of` (`the date` (c's `days without a guardian while under 18`) `days after` `the section 30 day`) `and` `the day before 21`
        IF (`the Part 2 last day of` c) `is after` `the day before 21`
        THEN `the Part 2 last day of` c
        OTHERWISE `the day before 21`
    WHERE
        `the section 30 day` MEANS `the anniversary` 6 `years after` (c's `claim accrual day`)
        `the day before 21` MEANS `the day before` (`the day of reaching age` 21 `for birth on` (c's `claimant birth day`))
        `the day before 25` MEANS `the day before` (`the day of reaching age` 25 `for birth on` (c's `claimant birth day`))

§§ `Part 3 Division 2 -- persons with a mental disability (ss 35-36)`

-- s 3(1): "mental disability ... means a disability ... an effect of which is that the person is unable to make
-- reasonable judgments in respect of matters relating to the person or the person's property" -- asked as a fact.
-- s 35(1): time during the disability in which the person "is without a guardian does not count"; (2) "Despite subsection
-- (1), an action ... cannot be commenced if 12 years have elapsed since the cause of action accrued." (3): subject to s 36.
-- s 36(1): a defendant in a close relationship during the disability: "cannot be commenced if 3 years have elapsed since
-- the relationship ceased"; (2) "does not apply if Part 2 Division 2 or 3 provides for a longer limitation period"; (3)
-- "Despite subsection (1), ... cannot be commenced if 30 years have elapsed since the cause of action accrued."
-- The s 35 suspension is applied to the Part 2 period and never shortens it (fork F5). Where the relationship has not
-- ceased, s 36(1) has not begun to run and only the 30 years of s 36(3) bound the time.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A DATE
`Division 2 -- the last day of` c MEANS
    IF c's `close relationship while disabled`
    THEN IF (`the Part 2 last day of` c) `is after` `the section 36 day`
         THEN `the Part 2 last day of` c
         ELSE `the earlier of` `the section 36 day` `and` `the 30 year day`
    ELSE `the later of` (`the Part 2 last day of` c) `and` (`the earlier of` (`the date` (c's `days without a guardian while disabled`) `days after` (`the Part 2 last day of` c)) `and` `the 12 year day`)
    WHERE
        `the 12 year day` MEANS `the anniversary` 12 `years after` (c's `claim accrual day`)
        `the 30 year day` MEANS `the anniversary` 30 `years after` (c's `claim accrual day`)
        `the section 36 day` MEANS
            IF c's `close relationship has ceased`
            THEN `the anniversary` 3 `years after` (c's `close relationship ceased on`)
            ELSE `the 30 year day`

§§ `The limitation period for the claim (ss 4, 6, 6A, 6B, 13-18, 30-36, 52, 53)`

-- s 4(1): "The limitation periods provided for under this Act apply only to causes of action that accrue on or after
-- commencement day." s 6(2): a personal injury cause of action accruing before then takes "that which would have applied
-- before commencement day" (not encoded).
-- s 6A(2): "Despite anything in this or any other Act, no limitation period applies in respect of a child sexual abuse
-- action"; s 90: "regardless of when the act or omission constituting child sexual abuse occurred".
-- s 6B(1): "no limitation period applies to a subsequent action for subsequent damages in respect of a subsequent dust
-- disease (as those terms are defined in the Civil Liability Act 2002 Part 2 Division 5)" -- asked as a fact.
-- s 52: under 18 at accrual and later with a mental disability: "the limitation period ... is the longer of those
-- limitation periods" (Division 1 or 2; s 7 is answered by its own question).
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the time limit for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the encoding covers` (c's `claim kind`))
        THEN `not answered by this encoding`
        IF c's `claim is a child sexual abuse action` AND (NOT (c's `claim kind` EQUALS `a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 action for a death`))
        THEN `no limitation period applies`
        IF c's `claim is a subsequent dust disease action`
        THEN `no limitation period applies`
        IF (c's `claim accrual day`) `is before` `the commencement day`
        THEN `the law before 15 November 2005 decides`
        IF `Division 1 extends the claim` c AND `Division 2 extends the claim` c
        THEN `the last day to commence is` (`the later of` (`Division 1 -- the last day of` c) `and` (`Division 2 -- the last day of` c))
        IF `Division 1 extends the claim` c
        THEN `the last day to commence is` (`Division 1 -- the last day of` c)
        IF `Division 2 extends the claim` c
        THEN `the last day to commence is` (`Division 2 -- the last day of` c)
        OTHERWISE `the last day to commence is` (`the Part 2 last day of` c)

§§ `Commencing in time -- a regulative rule (ss 12, 13-18)`

-- s 12(1): "the commencement of an action is ... the issue in the appropriate court of a writ or other originating
-- application". The bar "cannot be commenced if ... have elapsed" is modelled as what the plaintiff must do to keep the
-- action: MUST commence WITHIN the days from accrual to the last day, LEST the action is barred. The helper runs it over
-- the day of commencement (in the shape of the Civil Procedure Act 2010 (Vic) encoding's helper): on the stable l4 a
-- CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH, so FULFILLED means in time and anything else too late. It
-- takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Plaintiff` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff`

DECLARE `Commencing step` IS ONE OF
    `issue the writ or other originating application`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Plaintiff` `Commencing step`
`the action must be commenced within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the plaintiff`
    MUST `issue the writ or other originating application`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "the limitation period has expired: the action cannot be commenced unless a court extends the time (Part 3 Division 3) or the time was confirmed (Part 3 Division 5)"

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Plaintiff` `Commencing step`
      `the time of commencing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commencement satisfies` `the rule` `at` `the time of commencing` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of commencing`), (EVENT `the plaintiff` `issue the writ or other originating application` `the time of commencing`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether the action can be commenced on a day. JUST FALSE once the period has run ("cannot be commenced"); NOTHING
-- before accrual, under the old law, or outside the encoding (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text; limited by its own
-- wording).
GIVEN `the day of commencing` IS A DATE, c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the action can be commenced on` `the day of commencing` `for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time limit for` c
    WHEN `no limitation period applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the last day to commence is` `the final day` THEN
        IF `the day of commencing` `is before` (c's `claim accrual day`)
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF `the commencement satisfies` (`the action must be commenced within` (`the days from` (c's `claim accrual day`) `to` `the final day`)) `at` (`the days from` (c's `claim accrual day`) `to` `the day of commencing`)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 7 -- personal injury at birth, accrued before 15 November 2005`

-- s 7(1): "cause of action (childbirth) means a cause of action for damages relating to a personal injury to a person that
-- was incurred -- (a) in the course of the person's mother giving birth to the person; or (b) immediately after, and
-- arising from, the person's mother giving birth". (2): it "cannot be commenced if the cause of action accrued before
-- commencement day and -- (a) 6 years have elapsed since commencement day; or (b) the limitation period that would have
-- applied but for this section has expired." (3): subject to Part 3 except ss 30, 31 (and ss 32, 41 if 15 or over at
-- commencement day); (4): for Part 3 the cause is taken to have accrued on commencement day. The six years end on
-- 15 November 2011.
-- Not a childbirth cause of action: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording). Accrued on or after commencement
-- day: JUST FALSE (the "if" fails; the ordinary rules apply).
GIVEN `incurred in or immediately after my birth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accrued before 15 November 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the old period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of commencing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) -- the childbirth action cannot be commenced` `incurred in or immediately after my birth` `accrued before 15 November 2005` `the old period has expired` `the day of commencing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `incurred in or immediately after my birth`
        THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT `accrued before 15 November 2005`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the day of commencing` `is after` (`the anniversary` 6 `years after` `the commencement day`) OR `the old period has expired`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- extension by courts (ss 38-44)`

-- What a court may do on an extension application. The court's satisfaction and the s 44 matters (a fair trial, prejudice
-- to the defendant) are for the court; s 79(3): the plaintiff must prove the court should extend.
DECLARE `Court extension` IS ONE OF
    `the court may extend my time up to` HAS `the extended last day` IS A DATE
    `this section gives no extension on these facts`
    `this section does not reach my action`

-- s 38(2): "a court may extend the time ... up to 3 years from when the action ought reasonably to have been commenced if
-- the court is satisfied that the failure to commence the action was attributable to fraudulent or other improper conduct
-- of the defendant or a person for whom the defendant is vicariously liable." (4): not defamation.
GIVEN `the court is satisfied of fraud or improper conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I ought reasonably to have commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`s 38 -- extension for fraud or improper conduct` `the court is satisfied of fraud or improper conduct` `the day I ought reasonably to have commenced` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied of fraud or improper conduct`
    THEN `the court may extend my time up to` (`the anniversary` 3 `years after` `the day I ought reasonably to have commenced`)
    ELSE `this section gives no extension on these facts`

-- s 39(1), (2): an action for damages relating to a personal injury, or under the Fatal Accidents Act 1959. (3): the court
-- may extend "if the court is satisfied that, when the limitation period expired, a person to whom the cause of action
-- accrues -- (a) was not aware of the physical cause of the death or injury; (b) was aware of the physical cause ... but
-- was not aware that the death or injury was attributable to the conduct of a person; or (c) was aware of [both] ... but
-- after reasonable enquiry, had been unable to establish that person's identity." (4): "up to 3 years from when a person
-- to whom the cause of action accrues became aware, or ought reasonably to have become aware" of (a), (b) and (c).
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`
      `aware of the physical cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `aware it was caused by someone's conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knew who that person was` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made reasonable enquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I became aware of all three` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`s 39 -- extension for personal injury or death` k `aware of the physical cause` `aware it was caused by someone's conduct` `knew who that person was` `made reasonable enquiry` `the day I became aware of all three` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (k EQUALS `damages for a personal injury` OR k EQUALS `a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 action for a death`)
        THEN `this section does not reach my action`
        IF (NOT `aware of the physical cause`)
                OR (`aware of the physical cause` AND (NOT `aware it was caused by someone's conduct`))
                OR (`aware of the physical cause` AND `aware it was caused by someone's conduct` AND (NOT `knew who that person was`) AND `made reasonable enquiry`)
        THEN `the court may extend my time up to` (`the anniversary` 3 `years after` `the day I became aware of all three`)
        OTHERWISE `this section gives no extension on these facts`

-- s 41(1): "A plaintiff who was under 18 years of age when a cause of action accrued"; (2) "up to when the plaintiff
-- reaches 21 years of age"; (3) "A court is not to extend time ... unless the court is satisfied that in the circumstances
-- it was unreasonable for a guardian of the plaintiff not to commence the action within the limitation period". (4) not
-- defamation. The extended time ends the day before the 21st birthday (fork F2).
GIVEN `my birth day` IS A DATE
      `the accrual day` IS A DATE
      `the court is satisfied my guardian was unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`s 41 -- extension for a person under 18 with a guardian` `my birth day` `the accrual day` `the court is satisfied my guardian was unreasonable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the accrual day` `is before` (`the day of reaching age` 18 `for birth on` `my birth day`))
        THEN `this section does not reach my action`
        IF `the court is satisfied my guardian was unreasonable`
        THEN `the court may extend my time up to` (`the day before` (`the day of reaching age` 21 `for birth on` `my birth day`))
        OTHERWISE `this section gives no extension on these facts`

-- s 42(1): "A plaintiff who suffers a mental disability at any time after a cause of action accrues"; (2) "up to 12 years
-- from when the cause of action accrued"; (3) as s 41(3). (4) not defamation.
GIVEN `I have had a mental disability since accrual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accrual day` IS A DATE
      `the court is satisfied my guardian was unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`s 42 -- extension for a person with a mental disability with a guardian` `I have had a mental disability since accrual` `the accrual day` `the court is satisfied my guardian was unreasonable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I have had a mental disability since accrual`
        THEN `this section does not reach my action`
        IF `the court is satisfied my guardian was unreasonable`
        THEN `the court may extend my time up to` (`the anniversary` 12 `years after` `the accrual day`)
        OTHERWISE `this section gives no extension on these facts`

§§ `Part 3 Division 4 -- agreements (s 45)`

-- s 45(1): "Nothing in this Act prevents a person from agreeing to extend or shorten a limitation period". (2): a term "is
-- of no effect if it purports to -- (a) exclude the operation of section 33, 36 or 38; or (b) extinguish (rather than bar)
-- a right or title ... inconsistent with ... Part 5" (land; out of focus, asked with (a) as one fact).
GIVEN `it purports to exclude section 33, 36 or 38 or to extinguish a right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45 -- the agreed term has effect` `it purports to exclude section 33, 36 or 38 or to extinguish a right` MEANS
    IF `it purports to exclude section 33, 36 or 38 or to extinguish a right`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3 Division 5 -- confirmation (ss 46-50)`

-- s 46(1): a person confirms a cause of action if the person "(a) acknowledges ... person A's right or title, even though
-- the acknowledgment does not disclose a promise to pay; (b) makes ... a payment in relation to person B's right or title
-- ... in circumstances not inconsistent with an acknowledgment"; ((c), mortgages, out). s 48: "an acknowledgment is of
-- no effect unless it is in writing and signed by the maker." s 47: if the person confirms "(a) after the limitation
-- period ... begins to run; and (b) before that limitation period expires, the time during which the limitation period
-- runs before the confirmation is made does not count" for "a person having the benefit of the confirmation against a
-- person bound by the confirmation" (ss 49, 50). The period then runs afresh from the confirmation (fork F6). Applied to
-- the Part 2 period only (fork F7).
DECLARE `Kind of confirmation` IS ONE OF
    `a written acknowledgment of my right, signed by its maker`
    `an acknowledgment of my right that is not in writing, or not signed`
    `a payment to me in circumstances consistent with acknowledging my right`
    `no acknowledgment or payment`

DECLARE `Confirmation effect` IS ONE OF
    `time runs afresh and my new last day is` HAS `the new last day` IS A DATE
    `the confirmation does not extend my time`
    `not answered by this encoding for that kind of action`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of action`
      `the accrual day` IS A DATE
      `what was given` IS A `Kind of confirmation`
      `it binds the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Confirmation effect`
`ss 46-50 -- what the confirmation does` k `the accrual day` `what was given` `it binds the person I would sue` `the day it was given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the encoding covers` k)
        THEN `not answered by this encoding for that kind of action`
        IF `a confirmation` AND `it binds the person I would sue` AND (NOT (`the day it was given` `is before` `the accrual day`)) AND (NOT (`the day it was given` `is after` (`Part 2 -- the last day for` k `accrued on` `the accrual day`)))
        THEN `time runs afresh and my new last day is` (`the anniversary` (`the Part 2 period in years for` k) `years after` `the day it was given`)
        OTHERWISE `the confirmation does not extend my time`
    WHERE
        `a confirmation` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what was given`
            WHEN `a written acknowledgment of my right, signed by its maker` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a payment to me in circumstances consistent with acknowledging my right` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Part 4 Division 1 -- when a personal injury cause of action accrues (ss 55-57)`

DECLARE `Accrual` IS ONE OF
    `it accrued on` HAS `the day of accrual` IS A DATE
    `it has not yet accrued`
    `this Act does not say when it accrued`

-- s 55(1): "accrues when the only or earlier of such of the following events as are applicable occurs -- (a) the person
-- becomes aware that he or she has sustained a not insignificant personal injury; (b) the first symptom, clinical sign or
-- other manifestation of personal injury consistent with the person having sustained a not insignificant personal
-- injury." (2): not asbestos or silica dust.
-- s 56(1): asbestos or silica dust, "to a person who did not have knowledge of the relevant facts before 1 January 1984,
-- accrues when the person has knowledge of the relevant facts". Knowledge before 1984: neither s 55 nor s 56 applies
-- (NOTHING-kind: limited by its own wording).
-- s 57(1), (2): "If a person dies as a result of a personal injury ... but, immediately before the death, a cause of
-- action ... had not accrued under section 55 [56], the cause of action ... is to be taken as having accrued when the
-- person died."
GIVEN `it is from asbestos or silica dust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I became aware of a not insignificant injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I became aware` IS A DATE
      `a first sign appeared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the first sign` IS A DATE
      `I knew the relevant facts before 1984` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have knowledge of the relevant facts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I gained that knowledge` IS A DATE
      `the person died of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of death` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Accrual`
`ss 55-57 -- when the cause of action accrued` `it is from asbestos or silica dust` `I became aware of a not insignificant injury` `the day I became aware` `a first sign appeared` `the day of the first sign` `I knew the relevant facts before 1984` `I have knowledge of the relevant facts` `the day I gained that knowledge` `the person died of the injury` `the day of death` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is from asbestos or silica dust`
        THEN IF `I knew the relevant facts before 1984`
             THEN `this Act does not say when it accrued`
             ELSE `the accrual or death` `I have knowledge of the relevant facts` `the day I gained that knowledge`
        IF `I became aware of a not insignificant injury` AND `a first sign appeared`
        THEN `the accrual or death` TRUE (`the earlier of` `the day I became aware` `and` `the day of the first sign`)
        IF `I became aware of a not insignificant injury`
        THEN `the accrual or death` TRUE `the day I became aware`
        OTHERWISE `the accrual or death` `a first sign appeared` `the day of the first sign`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `an event happened` IS A BOOLEAN, `the event day` IS A DATE
        GIVETH AN `Accrual`
        `the accrual or death` `an event happened` `the event day` MEANS
            IF `an event happened` AND (NOT (`the person died of the injury` AND (`the event day` `is after` `the day of death`)))
            THEN `it accrued on` `the event day`
            ELSE IF `the person died of the injury`
                 THEN `it accrued on` `the day of death`
                 ELSE `it has not yet accrued`

-- s 56(3): "an injury is significant if the person whose knowledge is in question would reasonably have considered it
-- sufficiently serious to justify the person's commencing an action for damages against a defendant who did not dispute
-- liability and was able to satisfy a judgment." (4): an injury to which (4A) applies (a workers' compensation disability
-- or injury) "must not be treated as significant unless -- (a) the parties ... have so agreed; or (b) a medical panel ...
-- (i) has determined that the degree of the disability assessed in accordance with section 93D(2) of that Act is 30% or
-- more; or (ii) has assessed that the worker's degree of whole of person impairment ... is 25% or more; or (c) a Dust
-- Disease Medical Panel ... has determined ... that the degree of permanent whole of person impairment ... is at least
-- 25%." Both (3) and, where it applies, (4) must hold (fork F8).
DECLARE `Medical panel finding` IS ONE OF
    `no medical panel finding`
    `a 1981 Act medical panel degree of disability under s 93D(2)`
    `a 1981 Act medical panel degree of whole of person impairment under ss 146A and 146C`
    `a Dust Disease Medical Panel degree of permanent whole of person impairment under the 2023 Act`

GIVEN `it is serious enough to sue for` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a workers' compensation injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties agreed it is significant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the panel finding` IS A `Medical panel finding`
      `the percentage found` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(3), (4) -- the dust injury is significant` `it is serious enough to sue for` `it is a workers' compensation injury` `the parties agreed it is significant` `the panel finding` `the percentage found` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a workers' compensation injury` AND (NOT (`the parties agreed it is significant` OR `the panel threshold is met`))
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `it is serious enough to sue for`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the panel threshold is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the panel finding`
            WHEN `a 1981 Act medical panel degree of disability under s 93D(2)` THEN `the percentage found` AT LEAST 30
            WHEN `a 1981 Act medical panel degree of whole of person impairment under ss 146A and 146C` THEN `the percentage found` AT LEAST 25
            WHEN `a Dust Disease Medical Panel degree of permanent whole of person impairment under the 2023 Act` THEN `the percentage found` AT LEAST 25
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 56(2): "a person has knowledge of the relevant facts ... when the person has knowledge -- (a) that the injury in
-- question was significant; (b) that the injury was attributable in whole or in part to the act or omission which is
-- alleged to constitute the cause of action; (c) of the identity of the defendant; and (d) if it is alleged that the act or
-- omission was that of a person other than the defendant, of the identity of that person and the additional facts
-- supporting the bringing of an action against the defendant". (5): knowledge includes what the person might reasonably
-- have been expected to acquire (in the @desc). A "when" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `the injury is significant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I know the injury was caused by the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I know who the defendant is` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was someone else's` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I know who that was and the further facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 56(2) -- I have knowledge of the relevant facts` `the injury is significant` `I know the injury was caused by the act or omission` `I know who the defendant is` `the act was someone else's` `I know who that was and the further facts` MEANS
    IF `the injury is significant` AND `I know the injury was caused by the act or omission` AND `I know who the defendant is` AND ((NOT `the act was someone else's`) OR `I know who that was and the further facts`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 6 -- burden of proof and counterclaims (ss 79, 81)`

-- s 79(1): "a defendant ... has the burden of proving that the action cannot be commenced because the applicable
-- limitation period has expired." (2): "The plaintiff has the burden of proving that the time mentioned in section 32(1)
-- or 35(1) does not count". (3): "The plaintiff in an extension application has the burden of proving that a court should
-- extend the relevant limitation period."
DECLARE `Issue to prove` IS ONE OF
    `that the limitation period has expired`
    `that time without a guardian does not count`
    `that the court should extend the time`

DECLARE `Who must prove it` IS ONE OF
    `the defendant`
    `the plaintiff`

GIVEN `the issue` IS AN `Issue to prove`
GIVETH A `Who must prove it`
`s 79 -- who must prove it` `the issue` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the issue`
    WHEN `that the limitation period has expired` THEN `the defendant`
    OTHERWISE `the plaintiff`

-- s 81(1): "A counterclaim in an action (except a counterclaim solely by way of defence) is ... a separate action." (2):
-- against the plaintiff, "taken to have commenced ... when the defendant became a party to the action". (3): against a
-- person then joined, "when the other person is joined as a party to the counterclaim".
DECLARE `Counterclaim against` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff who sued me`
    `another person I joined to the counterclaim`

DECLARE `Counterclaim commencement` IS ONE OF
    `taken to have been commenced on` HAS `the day of commencement` IS A DATE
    `not a separate action`

GIVEN `it is solely a defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `against whom` IS A `Counterclaim against`
      `the day I became a party` IS A DATE
      `the day that person was joined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Counterclaim commencement`
`s 81 -- when my counterclaim is taken to commence` `it is solely a defence` `against whom` `the day I became a party` `the day that person was joined` MEANS
    IF `it is solely a defence`
    THEN `not a separate action`
    ELSE CONSIDER `against whom`
         WHEN `the plaintiff who sued me` THEN `taken to have been commenced on` `the day I became a party`
         WHEN `another person I joined to the counterclaim` THEN `taken to have been commenced on` `the day that person was joined`

§§ `Part 7 -- child sexual abuse actions barred or settled before 1 July 2018 (ss 89-92)`

-- s 89: "previously barred cause of action means a child sexual abuse cause of action that was statute barred immediately
-- before commencement day; previously settled cause of action means a child sexual abuse cause of action that was settled
-- after it was statute barred but before commencement day". s 91(1): an action on a previously barred cause of action
-- "may be commenced even though" it was barred, discontinued, or a judgment was given or it was dismissed on that ground.
-- s 92(2), (3): for a previously settled one, application for leave; the court may, if satisfied that it is just and
-- reasonable, grant leave and set aside the settlement agreement and any judgment giving effect to it.
DECLARE `Where Part 7 leaves my claim` IS ONE OF
    `I may commence it despite the earlier bar`
    `I need the court's leave, which may set aside the settlement`
    `Part 7 does not reopen a settlement made before the claim was barred`
    `no limitation period applies and Part 7 does not touch it`
    `it is not a child sexual abuse action`

GIVEN `it is a child sexual abuse action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was barred just before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was settled before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was barred when settled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where Part 7 leaves my claim`
`ss 89-92 -- where Part 7 leaves my claim` `it is a child sexual abuse action` `it was barred just before 1 July 2018` `it was settled before 1 July 2018` `it was barred when settled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a child sexual abuse action`
        THEN `it is not a child sexual abuse action`
        IF `it was settled before 1 July 2018`
        THEN IF `it was barred when settled`
             THEN `I need the court's leave, which may set aside the settlement`
             ELSE `Part 7 does not reopen a settlement made before the claim was barred`
        IF `it was barred just before 1 July 2018`
        THEN `I may commence it despite the earlier bar`
        OTHERWISE `no limitation period applies and Part 7 does not touch it`

-- s 91(2), (3): the court "may, if satisfied that it is just and reasonable to do so, set aside the previous judgment";
-- (6): "A court, other than the Supreme Court, may not set aside a previous judgment of another court."
GIVEN `the court is the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment was this court's own` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(3), (6) -- the court may set aside the earlier judgment` `the court is the Supreme Court` `the judgment was this court's own` `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the court is the Supreme Court`) AND (NOT `the judgment was this court's own`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the court is satisfied it is just and reasonable`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 92(7): amounts paid under a settlement "are taken to relate to the child sexual abuse ... to the extent of 50% if the
-- agreement -- (a) does not relate solely to that child sexual abuse; and (b) does not expressly deal with the extent to
-- which the agreement and amounts paid under it relate to that child sexual abuse." Otherwise the Act fixes no share
-- (NOTHING-kind: silent). (6): the court may take the amount into account if just and reasonable.
GIVEN `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `it related solely to the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it expressly dealt with the share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 92(7) -- the amount taken to relate to the abuse` `the amount paid` `it related solely to the abuse` `it expressly dealt with the share` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it related solely to the abuse`) AND (NOT `it expressly dealt with the share`)
    THEN JUST (`the amount paid` TIMES (50%))
    ELSE NOTHING
